2:T4b9,<p>There are so many kinds of voiceover work, such as <a href="https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk/commercial-voiceover" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" >commercial voiceover,</a> <a href="https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk/explainer-video-voice" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" >explainer videos, </a> <a href="https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk/movie-trailer-voice" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" >film trailer voiceover, </a> etc., but cartoon voiceover is usually held in the highest regard. Perhaps this is
because cartoons have given us many of our most beloved characters, such as Homer Simpson, Bugs
Bunny, Donald Duck, Lisa Simpson, Eric Cartman, Stewie Griffin, and so many more. If you’d like to
work on creating voiceover for memorable cartoon characters, then this guide is for you. And if
you’d like to hire Guy for your cartoon production, check out his <a href="https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk/character-voiceover" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" >character voiceover showreels</a> or
<a href="https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk/contact-guy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" >get in touch</a> to ask him to send over a free sample of your script.
</p>4:T492,<h2>Study the Drawings of Your Character</h2>
<p>When trying to pull a character’s voice out of thin air, it’s often helpful to study any drawings the
animators have of your character. Even if they haven’t made the animation yet, there will be plenty
of concept art for you to look at. Look at the character and consider where their voice is most likely
to come from. Their nose? Their throat? Deep down in their stomach? Take Santa Clause as an
example. <a href="https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk/santa-voice" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" title="Guy’s Santa voiceover">Guy’s Santa voiceover</a>  is deep and booming, as Santa has a rather round figure and he
looks like his voice would be just as big and round. It’s no coincidence that most people who perform
the voice of Santa opt for a deep voice that comes from the belly: this voice really fits the character’s
appearance. Similarly, if your character is a tiny little mouse, you should probably make your voice
high-pitched and nasal. Thinking about your cartoon character’s appearance can give you more than
enough information to come up with a believable voice for them.</p>7:["slug","cartoon-voiceover-guide","d"]
0:["T-vE3jocQsMrcy4PkMQjv",[[["",{"children":[["slug","cartoon-voiceover-guide","d"],{"children":["__PAGE__?{\"slug\":\"cartoon-voiceover-guide\"}",{}]}]},"$undefined","$undefined",true],["",{"children":[["slug","cartoon-voiceover-guide","d"],{"children":["__PAGE__",{},[["$L1",[[["$","script","schema-0",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BlogPosting\",\"@id\":\"https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk/cartoon-voiceover-guide#blogposting\",\"mainEntityOfPage\":\"https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk/cartoon-voiceover-guide\",\"headline\":\"Cartoon Voiceover Guide\",\"url\":\"https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk/cartoon-voiceover-guide\",\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\":\"Guy Harris\",\"url\":\"https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk/voiceoverguy\",\"image\":\"https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk/images/guy-harris-profile.jpg\"},\"publisher\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"VoiceoverGuy\",\"url\":\"https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk\",\"logo\":{\"@type\":\"ImageObject\",\"url\":\"https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk/assets/images/guy-harris-voiceover.webp\"}},\"inLanguage\":\"en-GB\",\"isAccessibleForFree\":true,\"description\":\"Cartoon Voiceover Guide: Creating memorable characters - A great bog on how to come up with the different voices for the many projects you will be asked for.\",\"image\":{\"@type\":\"ImageObject\",\"url\":\"https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk/assets/img/blog/cartoon-voiceover-guide2.jpg\"}}"}}],["$","script","schema-1",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"@id\":\"https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk/cartoon-voiceover-guide#breadcrumb\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"News & Blog\",\"item\":\"https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk/voiceover-news\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"Cartoon Voiceover Guide\",\"item\":\"https://www.voiceoverguy.co.uk/cartoon-voiceover-guide\"}]}"}}]],["$","div",null,{"className":"page-header","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container page-header-nav-wrap","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"page-header-content","children":[["$","h1",null,{"children":"Cartoon Voiceover Guide"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"page-header-sub","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$2"}}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"page-header-arrows","children":[["$","$L3",null,{"href":"/which-recording-studio-software-is-best","className":"page-header-arrow","title":"The Best Recording Studio Software?","aria-label":"Previous: The Best Recording Studio Software?","children":"‹"}],["$","$L3",null,{"href":"/top-5-films-that-use-voice-over-narration-perfectly","className":"page-header-arrow","title":"Voice-over Narration in Movies","aria-label":"Next: Voice-over Narration in Movies","children":"›"}]]}]]}]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"blog-post-body","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-post-main one-col","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-text-col","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"<h2>Watch Lots of Cartoons</h2>\r\n<p>The first thing you should do is watch a lot of cartoons! But don’t just watch them, listen to them\r\ntoo. Listen to the different voices and imagine the voiceover artist sitting in a recording studio\r\nperforming. Keep a pen and paper handy and make notes on the various voices you hear. Note down\r\nwhen something sounds good and why, but also make note of when it doesn’t sound good; you can\r\nlearn as much from people’s mistakes as from their successes!</p>\r\n"}}],false,false]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-post-section two-col","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-media-col","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-post-img-card","children":[["$","img",null,{"src":"/assets/img/blog/cartoon-voiceover-guide2.jpg","alt":"Cartoon Voiceover Guide: Creating memorable characters","className":"blog-post-img"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"blog-post-img-caption","children":"Cartoon Voiceover Guide"}]]}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-text-col","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"<h2>Think About Range Rather Than Gender</h2>\r\n<p>Bart Simpson is one of the most famous cartoon characters of all time. Bart is the quintessential\r\nnaughty little boy, yet he’s voiced by a woman. Comedian and voiceover actress Nancy Cartwright is\r\nthe voice of Bart Simpson and fans of the show would be forgiven for not realising that Bart wasn’t\r\nvoiced by a young boy. Cartwright’s vocal pitch and intonation is perfect for Bart Simpson; your voice\r\nmight be a good fit for someone who looks completely different to you, so make sure you keep an\r\nopen mind.</p>"}}]]}],[["$","div","0",{"className":"blog-post-section two-col","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-text-col","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"<h2>Try a Bad Impersonation of a Famous Person</h2>\r\n<p>A good shortcut to finding a voice full of personality is to attempt an impression a famous person or\r\ncharacter. Stewie from Family Guy was loosely based on Rex Harrison, and Stimpy from Ren &amp;\r\nStimpy was based on Peter Lorre. Find an actor or actress who already has lots of character and try\r\nan exaggerated impression of them. Even if your impression isn’t very good, the attempt has\r\nprobably pushed your voice in several interesting ways, giving you a really distinctive voice.</p>"}}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-media-col","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"/assets/img/blog/cartoon-voiceover-guide3.jpg","alt":"Cartoon Voiceover Guide: Creating memorable characters","className":"blog-post-img"}]}]]}],["$","div","1",{"className":"blog-post-section two-col","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-media-col","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"/assets/img/blog/cartoon-voiceover-guide4.jpg","alt":"Cartoon Voiceover Guide: Creating memorable characters","className":"blog-post-img"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-text-col","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$4"}}]]}],["$","div","2",{"className":"blog-post-section two-col","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-text-col","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"<h2>Think About Your Character’s Personality</h2>\r\n<p>The last thing that makes a huge difference to any cartoon character’s voice is their personality.\r\nHomer Simpson is a donut-eating, beer-guzzling buffoon, but he’s also a sweet man, underneath it\r\nall. Homer’s voice captures his personality perfectly. However, if you watch some of the early\r\nSimpsons episodes, you’ll notice that Dan Castellaneta hadn’t quite honed his Homer Simpson voice\r\nyet. It was almost right, but it lacked depth; it sounded like a cartoonish impression of Homer. As\r\ntime went on, Castellaneta got to know Homer a lot better and he was able to give him a much more\r\nnuanced voice as a result. Think about your character’s personality. Think about their lifestyle and\r\ntheir relationships with the other characters. The better you know your character, the easier it will\r\nbe for you to give them a truly unique voice.</p>"}}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-media-col","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"/assets/img/blog/cartoon-voiceover-guide5.jpg","alt":"Cartoon Voiceover Guide: Creating memorable characters","className":"blog-post-img"}]}]]}]],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-bottom-text","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"<br><p>That’s it for this cartoon voiceover guide. Cartoon voiceover is an incredibly rewarding job and often\r\nthe voiceover actor’s enjoyment is clearly evident from their performance. If you enjoy yourself,\r\nyou’ll perform better, so make sure you have fun!</p>"}}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-post-cta","children":["$","$L3",null,{"href":"/voiceover-news","className":"cta-btn cta-btn--outline","children":"← Back to News & Blog"}]}],["$","$L5",null,{"pageTitle":"Cartoon Voiceover Guide","pageUrl":"cartoon-voiceover-guide"}]]}]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"blog-related-strip","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-related-grid","children":[["$","$L3","633",{"href":"/world-of-warships-tutorial-voice","className":"blog-related-card","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-related-img-wrap","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"/assets/img/blog/world-of-warships-tutorial-voice.jpg","alt":"World of Warships Tutorial Voice","className":"blog-related-img"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-related-title","children":"World of Warships Tutorial Voice"}]]}],["$","$L3","852",{"href":"/voiceover-vox-award-winner-2018","className":"blog-related-card","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-related-img-wrap","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"/assets/img/blog/voiceover-vox-award-winner-2019.jpg","alt":"voiceover-vox-award-winner-2019","className":"blog-related-img"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-related-title","children":"Voiceover Vox Award Winner 2018"}]]}],["$","$L3","986",{"href":"/draw-slasher-voice","className":"blog-related-card","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-related-img-wrap","children":["$","img",null,{"src":"/assets/img/blog/draw-slasher-game-voiceover.jpg","alt":"Draw Slasher Game Voiceover – Trailer and Character Voices","className":"blog-related-img"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-related-title","children":"Draw Slasher Game Voiceover"}]]}]]}]}]}]],null],null],null]},[null,["$","$L6",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","$7","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L8",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":"$undefined","notFoundStyles":"$undefined"}]],null]},[[[["$","link","0",{"rel":"stylesheet","href":"/_next/static